  "status_text": "Helper switches can shorten a proof, and Lean checked the cost of supplying them. Give each pigeon a short list of holes, with one pigeon too many. A circuit must fill in the helper switches for every setting of the original bits. On the checked family, a polynomial-length proof in termwise Res(k,+) with fixed k forces at least linearly many two-input AND and OR gates in that circuit, with parity and NOT free. Lean checked a construction on the same family with linear circuit size and a linear number of lines of ordinary resolution (L-pcx-366).",
